"""
Binds a count shared by the whole process, for numbers that must never repeat.

- It keeps the count in C with @embed, so it is an unsafe module.
- Standard.Graph is the safe module built on it.
- The count holds when tasks on several threads call it at once.
- After the largest Nat64 the count wraps round to 0, which the caller must refuse.

    let serial: Nat64 := nextSerial();
"""
pragma Targets(Names => "linux openbsd freebsd darwin wasm");
module Bindings.Serial is
    """
    A number that no earlier call in this process returned: 1 on the first
    call, then 2, and so on, also when tasks on several threads call it at
    once.  After the largest Nat64 the count wraps round and the call
    returns 0, which the caller must refuse.
    No contract: a binding to C; the safe module built on it states the contracts.
    """
    function nextSerial(): Nat64;
end module.
